==Greek==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|el|grc|μήτηρ||mother}}, from {{inh|el|grk-pro|*mā́tēr}}, from {{inh|el|ine-pro|*méh₂tēr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/miˈtera/|lang=el}}

===Noun===
{{el-noun|f|μητέρες|m=πατέρας}}

# [[mother]]
#: {{ux|el|inline=1|η '''μητέρα''' του μαθητή|the student's mother}}
# {{lb|el|figuratively}} [[mother]] {{gloss|the first example of something}}
#: {{ux|el|inline=1|η '''μητέρα''' των κοινοβουλίων|the mother of parliaments}}
# {{lb|el|figuratively|colloquial}} [[mother]] {{gloss|something that is the greatest of its kind}}
#: {{ux|el|inline=1|Ήταν '''μητέρα''' των μαχών.|It was the mother of battles.}}

